{"additions":579,"author":{"id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMTA5NDkz","is_bot":false,"login":"td72","name":"Kohei Hosokawa"},"body":"## Summary\n\nCloses #169.\n\n- **`domain/graphql.rs`** replaces `gh project field-list` / `item-list` for the board fetch with two `gh api graphql` requests that ask only for what the page renders:\n  1. the project's **fields** (name / type / single-select options), **saved views** (the same selection as before) and the **item count**;\n  2. the **items** in pages of up to 100, `first` sized to that count (capped at `ITEM_LIMIT`), each with `fieldValues(first: 30)` covering text / number / date / single-select / iteration / labels / users / milestone / repository / linked PRs.\n- Responses are reshaped into the exact `gh … --format json` layout (`title` / `status` / `content`, other values under their lowercased-first-letter key, labels / assignees / linked PRs as arrays, milestone and iteration as objects, repository as its URL), so `ProjectItem` / `ProjectField` and every pane stay untouched. User and organization roots, draft and redacted items handled as before.\n- The CLI path remains as the **fallback** when the GraphQL path fails; view parsing is shared (`views_from`), and every response's `rateLimit` feeds the header's quota display.\n\n## Measured cost (demo board, 8 items, 15 fields)\n\n| Request | Points |\n|---|---|\n| fields + views + count | 1 |\n| items (`first: 8`) | 2 |\n| **per board** | **3** (was ~50 after #163, ~200 before) |\n| a full `first: 100` page | 31 |\n\n## Docs\n\nGuide Projects chapter (en/ja) and both READMEs describe the GraphQL fetch and its cost; the client module comment lists the fallback.\n\n## Tests\n\nFixture-driven conversion tests for fields (types, options), views (unknown layouts skipped) and items (every value type, draft, redacted, unknown value types dropped), plus query-shape checks. 390 tests green, clippy clean. No GIF changes — the rendered data is identical.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01TreGn5Xh4PjDRv9Yo4QU4w","changedFiles":7,"comments":[],"createdAt":"2026-09-08T09:34:48Z","deletions":126,"headRefName":"feat/projects-graphql-board","labels":[],"number":173,"reviewDecision":"","reviews":[{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABMl5nQQ","author":{"login":"copilot-pull-request-reviewer"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"### 🟡 Changes recommended\n\nThere are correctness and documentation issues in the new GraphQL path (variable typing in `run()` and hard caps that can truncate fields/values) plus Japanese doc punctuation/wording problems that should be fixed before approval.\n\n*Once you've addressed the issues Copilot identified, you can request another Copilot review.*\n\n<details>\n<summary>Pull request overview</summary>\n\nThis PR reduces GitHub Projects (v2) board fetch GraphQL cost by replacing `gh project field-list` / `item-list` with a purpose-built `gh api graphql` flow in the Projects domain, while keeping the existing `ProjectItem` / `ProjectField` shapes so the UI panes remain unchanged.\n\n**Changes:**\n- Added a new GraphQL-based board fetcher that reshapes responses into the existing `gh … --format json`-like structures.\n- Updated the Projects domain client to prefer the GraphQL path and fall back to the `gh project` CLI path on failure; views parsing is shared.\n- Updated user-facing docs (en/ja) to describe the new GraphQL-based board fetch and its cost characteristics.\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>File summaries</summary>\n\n| File | Description |\r\n| ---- | ----------- |\r\n| src/projects/domain/mod.rs | Registers the new `graphql` domain module. |\r\n| src/projects/domain/graphql.rs | Implements the GraphQL queries + response reshaping, including conversion tests. |\r\n| src/projects/domain/client.rs | Switches `fetch_board` to GraphQL-first with CLI fallback; reuses `views_from`. |\r\n| README.md | Updates Projects View description to mention GraphQL fetch. |\r\n| docs/README.ja.md | Updates Japanese README Projects View description for GraphQL (needs wording/accuracy fixes per comments). |\r\n| docs/guide/src/views-projects.md | Updates the Projects guide (en) to describe the new GraphQL fetch approach/cost. |\r\n| docs/guide/ja/src/views-projects.md | Updates the Projects guide (ja) similarly (needs wording/parentheses fix per comments). |\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>Review details</summary>\n\n- **Files reviewed:** 7/7 changed files\n- **Comments generated:** 3\n- **Review effort level:** Lite\n</details>\n\n---\n\n💡 <a href=\"/td72/vig/new/main?filename=.github/skills/code-review/SKILL.md\" class=\"Link--inTextBlock\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Add a `code-review` agent skill</a> or configure MCP servers for context-aware, tailored reviews. <a href=\"https://docs.github.com/copilot/how-tos/use-copilot-agents/request-a-code-review/use-code-review?tool=webui#mcp-servers-and-agent-skills\" class=\"Link--inTextBlock\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Learn more in the docs.</a>","submittedAt":"2026-09-08T09:39:13Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"87e0c1ace40af048fcb838960bd5e153dfdbfabb"}},{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABMl9U1w","author":{"login":"td72"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"","submittedAt":"2026-09-08T09:44:32Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"87e0c1ace40af048fcb838960bd5e153dfdbfabb"}},{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABMl9WTw","author":{"login":"td72"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"","submittedAt":"2026-09-08T09:44:34Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"d9ddfb2d46f5fd99db5ddd0d91799605684b7a48"}},{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABMl9YJQ","author":{"login":"td72"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"","submittedAt":"2026-09-08T09:44:36Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"d9ddfb2d46f5fd99db5ddd0d91799605684b7a48"}},{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABMmAGzQ","author":{"login":"copilot-pull-request-reviewer"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"### 🔵 Needs a closer look\n\nThere are user-facing documentation typos in updated text that should be corrected before merging.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Review details</summary>\n\n### Suppressed comments (2)\n\n**Previously missed (2)** — in code that hasn't changed since the last review.\n\n**docs/guide/ja/src/views-projects.md:7**\n* Japanese guide text has a duplicated phrase (\"ボードは ボード本体は\") and the parenthetical reads unnaturally. This looks like an editing mistake in the Projects View intro sentence.\n**src/projects/domain/graphql.rs:5**\n* Module doc comment has a grammatical typo: \"a fields + 3-item probe\" reads like a missing word and makes the cost explanation harder to parse.\n\n- **Files reviewed:** 7/7 changed files\n- **Comments generated:** 0 new\n- **Review effort level:** Lite\n</details>","submittedAt":"2026-09-08T09:48:37Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"d9ddfb2d46f5fd99db5ddd0d91799605684b7a48"}}],"state":"MERGED","statusCheckRollup":[{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-09-08T10:00:58Z","conclusion":"SKIPPED","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/34213161906/job/102018675438","name":"create-tag","startedAt":"2026-09-08T10:01:04Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Release"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-09-08T09:45:57Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/34211675996/job/102013893624","name":"build (x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu, ubuntu-latest)","startedAt":"2026-09-08T09:44:39Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Build"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-09-08T09:45:14Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/34211675973/job/102013893491","name":"lint","startedAt":"2026-09-08T09:44:38Z","status":"COMPLETED","wo